    "narrative": "For today's matchup, our core offensive engine is powered by the elite speed-power combination of **Trea Turner** (77.53) and **Kyle Schwarber** (76.68). Both benefit significantly from a favorable park factor and a matchup against Bradish, whose 4.26 xERA provides a green light for aggressive starting. **Trea Turner** remains our highest-ceiling asset, as his stolen base potential mitigates the risks posed by Bradish\u2019s hold-runner efficiency. Meanwhile, **Yordan Alvarez** (73.79) remains a must-start despite the neutral park, as his elite xwOBA of 0.476 renders the matchup against Rocker almost irrelevant. **Lars Nootbaar** (65.16) also deserves recognition; while his base projection is modest, the favorable platoon split against Scherzer and the top-of-the-order positioning make him a strong play in the outfield.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Chase Meidroth**, who finished just shy of our 40.0 floor with a score of 36.63. While his profile is intriguing, the combination of a difficult matchup against Jax and his lower-order batting position (7th) suppressed his efficiency score below our threshold for starting. Elsewhere, we continue to monitor the status of **Hyeseong Kim**, **Christian Yelich**, and **Colt Keith**, who remain sidelined and unavailable to bolster our depth today. On the active side, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (65.35) makes the cut as our UTIL option despite a challenging matchup against Cole; his leadoff role and platoon advantage outweigh the risks posed by the current wind conditions, which were the primary reason for his slight score regression. \n\nWe are proceeding with caution regarding **Dillon Dingler** (62.06) and **Junior Caminero** (65.48), as both face left-handed pitching; however, their respective order spots and favorable xwOBA metrics keep them securely in our lineup. While **Carson Benge** (57.29) is at the bottom of our starters, he is still preferred over the reserves like **Chase Meidroth** due to his projected plate appearances. We are keeping a close watch on **Gary Sanchez**, **Nelson Velazquez**, **Casey Schmitt**, **Josh Smith**, **Jacob Gonzalez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Pedro Ramirez** to ensure no late-breaking lineup changes force a pivot. Keep the rotation tight; our goal remains maximizing daily efficiency while protecting our game caps.",
